          <Pad Id="XITqkfZZlVNGNHxZqGGJkg" Comment="Title" Bounds="182,501,190,19" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="HowTo Draw a Line">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="qUDab2emnzSTmYLkOG000k" Bounds="85,594,830,192" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- A Line is drawn only with a Stroke Width above 0. Points are in units of the Renderer Space (1 unit = 100 DIP, origin top left), in the space of the parent.&#xD;&#xA;- Trim takes fractions of the length: Trim Start 0 and Trim End 1 draw everything. Here an LFO drives Trim End, so the line draws itself; Trim Offset shifts the window along the line. Animating Trim costs far less than changing the points.&#xD;&#xA;- Dash (lengths of dashes and gaps) and Dash Offset make a dashed stroke.&#xD;&#xA;- A shape holds at most 8190 points (a Line has 2). Polylines whose points change every frame should stay below about 4000 points.&#xD;&#xA;- Connect it to Renderer [Qt] or a Group [Qt].">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
